If you are at this stage, get a good magnifier and examine the system 
board for faults. Objects or i/o cards that have been clumsily dropped 
onto the board can bend and short adjacent chip pinouts, Also metalic 
whiskers shorting pins or just minute damage in general. Pay particular 
attention to any chip with fine pitch leadouts. The other thing to try 
is to remove the system board and flex very gently (I mean *very* genty, 
only a few degrees) from end to end. This can pick up marginal bga 
joints enough to get the board working, but is obviously not a permanent 
solution for anything other than hobby use...

Chris


