On Fri, 5 Jan 2007, Bill Gunshannon wrote:

>> Some of it were even in the 8080 and the Z80.
>
> What "string" and "BCD" support was in the Z80 or the 8080?

8080:
DAA (Decimal adjust Acc)
-- after a BCD addition/subtraction.  There's a flag that notes whether 
the last arithmetic operation was an addition or a subtraction.

8085:
DAA -- same as 8085

Z80:
BCD support:
DAA -- same as 8080
RLD -- rotate left digit
RRD -- rotate right digit

RLD/RRD rotate the three nibbles in the lower part of the Accumulator (A) 
and whatever byte in memory HL points to.  The upper nibble of A is 
untouched.


Block scan:
CPD -- compare and decrement
CPDR -- compare, decrement, and repeat
CPI -- compare and increment
CPIR -- compare, increment, and repeat

cmp A and (HL) (i.e. perform A-(HL), discard result but keep flags)
increment/decrement HL
decrement BC
maybe loop until BC == 0 or A was equal to (HL), that is until Z is set.


Block copy/fill
LDD  -- load and decrement
LDDR -- load, decrement, and repeat
LDI  -- load and increment
LDIR -- load, increment, and repeat

(DE) <-- (HL)
increment/decrement DE and HL
decrement BC
maybe loop until BC == 0

This can be used to fill blocks as well.  There are faster ways to block 
fill but they require tricks such as relocating the stack to the end of 
the block to be filled and then pushing lots of register pairs.


Port I/O:
IND  -- input and decrement
INDR -- input, decrement, and repeat
INI  -- input and increment
INIR -- input, increment, and repeat

(HL) <-- read from port C
increment/decrement HL
decrement B
maybe loop until B == 0


OTDR -- output, decrement, and repeat
OTIR -- output, increment, and repeat
OUTD -- output and decrement
OUTI -- output and increment

output (HL) to port C
increment/decrement HL
decrement B
maybe loop until B == 0


8051, thrown in as a bonus:
DA	A -- Decimal-adjust Accumulator for Addition
SWAP	  -- swap nibbles within the Accumulator

-Peter


